Dome Connect — native KDE Connect protocol backend
=================================================

This is a local fork of GSConnect 74, upstream commit
61cc76b966f95a19d396fe0fc42a755fcb902bd4. Protocol, device and plugin code
retain their upstream licenses and attribution. The GNOME extension sources
are retained for reference; they are neither built nor installed by default.

The installed service is a Gio.Application running under GJS. Its separate
FLTK dialog helper follows DomeD appearance settings and supports native
Wayland. No installed module imports Gtk or Gdk. The existing DomeD FLTK
connected-device controls use a compatibility subset of org.kde.kdeconnect.
This is a new implementation, not a build flag that removes Qt from KDE's
original daemon. Qt is fundamental to that daemon's object and I/O model.

Build as the regular user in the de-xr workspace:

    meson setup build --prefix=/usr/local
    meson compile -C build
    meson test -C build --print-errorlogs
    DESTDIR="$PWD/stage" meson install -C build --no-rebuild

All C++ code uses CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release. The FLTK build at
/opt/fltk-vr/toolkit and shared appearance headers in ../flterm-xr/xr are
required. The --no-rebuild install copies the user-built staging tree; do
not compile with sudo. The RPM builder is tools/package-domed.py BUILD_DIR.
It produces a system-integrated package with no Qt/GTK requirements.

Runtime dependencies: GJS, GIO/GLib and its TLS backend, OpenSSL, Python Gio,
wl-clipboard, pactl, pw-play, SSHFS/OpenSSH, and ydotool. Only the dialog helper
links FLTK. D-Bus activation, autostart and command wrappers retain the old
KDE Connect entry points. No desktop or display manager restart is required.

Implemented paths include LAN discovery, pinned TLS, explicit pairing, ping,
phone battery, file/text sharing, clipboard, find-phone, SFTP, media/system
volume, notifications, SMS, remote commands and native input adapters. Tests
cover protocol and plugin behavior; they do not establish complete UI or API
parity with every KDE Connect feature. Bluetooth transport is not implemented;
it was already disabled on the target system. Notification forwarding and
remote keyboard behavior depend on compositor permissions. ydotool uses a
private per-user socket and existing /dev/uinput access; no global device
permissions are changed.

Migration reads ~/.config/kdeconnect, copies the local identity to the private
~/.config/kdeconnect-dome directory, imports trusted peer pins, and preserves
original files. It never silently accepts pairing or replaces a changed peer
certificate. Existing paired devices reconnect without re-pairing. Automatic
migration runs once; subsequent unpairing remains authoritative.

SFTP mounts use the local identity key and the paired Android TLS certificate's
public key as an SSH host pin. Android deliberately uses the same keypair for
its SSH server. Pins live in the private application configuration directory;
the user's SSH agent, SSH config and global known_hosts are not modified.
Password-only peers or peers with a distinct SSH host identity fail explicitly.
Mounts are private under $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/kdeconnect-dome/DEVICE/files and are
unmounted on disconnect. Busy mounts are not forcibly detached.

Validation:
- tools/test-domed.py BUILD_DIR: upstream protocol/plugin suites, isolated bus
  and settings, GTK imports removed from fixture initialization only.
- tools/test-wire.py RUNTIME: independent Python TLS peer, explicit pairing,
  certificate changes, CLI, Unicode text, real SSHFS against local OpenSSH,
  rejection of an SSH host-key mismatch, unchanged global SSH trust, and
  process mappings without Qt or GTK. Requires user-runnable sshd and /dev/fuse.
- tools/test-dialogs.py RUNTIME: isolated Xvfb, real GJS-to-FLTK UTF-8 and cancel
  responses. The production helper defaults to native Wayland through FLTK.

Session authentication for installation is handled by sudo/askpass. Runtime
certificates, user device data and credentials must never be checked into Git.
